course: dictionary
lesson: 11826
title: Cutting in half: bisection
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A bisection is the act of dividing something into two equal parts. Look at the word: it is about cutting in two. «Ravi folded the paper so both ends met exactly, making a bisection of the sheet.» Each half is the same size, so the fold is a bisection.
explain: In geometry, you can make a bisection with a compass and a ruler. «Mia used her compass to make a bisection of the line, so both sides were 5 cm long.» The line is cut at its exact middle, and neither side is longer than the other.
explain: In computing, bisection means something different. It is a method of finding an answer by halving a range again and again. «Guess my number between 1 and 100» is a bisection game: guess 50, then keep the half where the answer must be. Each guess cuts the range in half, so you find the number quickly. This is also called a binary search.
fact: Bisection means dividing something into two equal parts.
fact: In maths, a bisection can split a line or an angle exactly in half.
fact: In computing, bisection means halving a range again and again to find an answer.
fact: The bisection method is also called a binary search.
fact: With bisection, guessing a number from 1 to 100 takes at most 7 guesses.
exercise: Ravi folded the paper so both ends met exactly. What did the fold make? | A pile of tiny pieces | *Two equal parts, a bisection | A triangle with three sides | A curve with no ends
exercise: In the game «guess my number between 1 and 100», you guess 50 first and keep halving the range. What method is this? | *Bisection | Spelling | Rounding | Multiplication
exercise: Which word means dividing something into two equal parts? | Adding | Doubling | *Bisection | Rounding
test: Sam says the bisection of 10 is 4 and 6. Is he right? | No, a bisection gives 2 and 8 | *No, a bisection gives 5 and 5 | Yes, because 4 and 6 add up to 10 | Yes, 4 and 6 are equal
test: In a binary search, what happens after each guess? | The guesses are random | *The range is halved and the half with the answer is kept | The range doubles | The game ends straight away
exam: What is a bisection in maths? | Counting the sides of a shape | Measuring the length of a line with a ruler | Joining two shapes into one | *Dividing something into two equal parts
